# edge_diag_rules.c, Cloud, 2026-10-29 (CL642). Predictions written before the run:
# # DQ-024 block, Cloud, written before any run (block start in block_start.txt)
# 
# Hand derivation (from the kit's R_step, S_rule, antiperiod, half_black): with g_j = R_(j-1) OR R_(j-2), R_j = running XOR of g_j,
# d_j = e_j - e_(j-1) = parity of the weight of g_j over one period P = p_(j-1).
#  Case A (d_(j-1) = 1, R_(j-1) antiperiodic with antiperiod P/2): weight(g_j over P) = 2 w(R_(j-2)) + (P/2 - w(R_(j-2)))
#    so d_j = parity of w(R_(j-2)) over its least period p_(j-2) = P/2 (P >= 4). If d_(j-2) = 1 that weight is P/4, even: no_three.
#  Case B (d_(j-1) = 0): d_j = omega_(j-1) + omega_(j-2) + parity of w(R_(j-1) AND R_(j-2)) over P, with omega = weight parity over the period.
#  Weight parity of a non-doubling R_j over its period: omega_j = parity of the number of black cells of g_j at EVEN times in one period.
# Fair model: every unforced d_j a fair coin, the only constraint no_three: stationary density of doublings = 3/7 = 0.4286.
#  (Markov chain on (d_(j-1), d_(j-2)): pi(00) = pi(01) = pi(10) = 2/7, pi(11) = 1/7; density = pi(10) + pi(11) = 3/7.)
# This COMPETES with DQ-024's conjecture (density 1/2): the kit's "0.43 j" and my e_79/79 = 0.43 fit 3/7; the recent marginal rate 0.46 fits neither cleanly.
# 
# Predictions, before the run:
#  P1 (exact): the Case A rule d_j = [w(R_(j-2)) odd] holds for every j <= 50 with d_(j-1) = 1, d_(j-2) = 0. Counterfactual: one failure kills the derivation.
#  P2 (exact): for every non-doubling j <= 50 (j >= 3), omega_j = parity of even-time black cells of g_j over one period.
#  P3 (statistical): over j <= 92 (e_j from my J_k to 38 and Rowland's to 40), the conditional doubling frequencies given (d_(j-1), d_(j-2)) in {00, 01, 10}
#     are each within 0.15 of 1/2 (the fair model). Counterfactual: all three at or above 0.60 (what the density-1/2 conjecture needs).
#  PU (unexpected check): the Case B AND-parity term: report its frequency of being 1; the fair model has no prediction for it, a strong bias would point at structure.
# Record searched: S_rule, no_three, antiperiod, half_black, per_upper_half, DQ-024, GC2003 (even-tick parity), 3/7 (none).
# Caps: Cloud CPU, one process, under a minute, 128-bit C, j <= 50 (periods <= 2^22).
